0,Miskito language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miskito_language,"March 4, 2026 - With around 150,000 speakers, Miskito is the most widely spoken of a family of languages of Nicaragua and Honduras that has come to be known as Misumalpan. This name is formed from parts of the names of the family's subgroups: Miskito, Sumo, Matagalpan. The relationship of some aspects of the ...",Mískito,Misumalpan
1,Misumalpan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Misumalpan,"November 11, 2025 - The Misumalpan languages (also Misumalpa or Misuluan) are a small family of languages spoken by different ethnic groups in Mosquitia. The name ""Misumalpan"" was devised by John Alden Mason and is composed of syllables from the names of the family's three members Miskito, Sumo languages and ...",Mískito,Misumalpan
2,Miskito people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miskito_people,"May 24, 2026 - The majority of Miskitos speak their native Miskito language. The Miskito language is a part of the Misumalpan language family. Some villages also speak Sumu, a closely related language within these ethnic groups. In addition, many Miskitos have adopted figures of speech from English and Spanish ...",Mískito,Misumalpan
3,Misumalpan languages - WikipediaMúsica Miskita - YouTube MusicMiskito language - WikipediaMusic of the Miskito Indians of Honduras and NicaraguaMiskito Music - VideosFE 4237 Music of the Miskito Indians of Honduras and ...,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Misumalpan_languages,"The Misumalpan languages (also Misumalpa or Misuluan) are a small family of languages spoken by different Indigenous groups in the region commonly known as Mosquitia, referred to in Miskitu as Yapti Tasba Masrka (“the People’s Land”). See full list on en.wikipedia.org Listen to Música Miskita on YouTube Music - a dedicated music app with official songs, music videos, remixes, covers, and more. Miskito (Miskitu in the Miskito language) is a Misumalpan language spoken by the Miskito people in northeastern Nicaragua, especially in the North Caribbean Coast Autonomous Region, and in eastern Honduras. ""First contacted from the outside world by Columbus on his fourth and final voyage in 1502, the Miskito Indians have been able to maintain their culture despite the influx of a variety of different races by absorbing and integrating newcomers into their society. Himno Nacional en Miskito Duration: 1:00 12.9K views | Oct 28, 2017 Baile Miskito Nicaragua Duration: 4:46 17.2K views | Mar 29, 2013 Música miskita Chelmor Calderón ft Auner Panting Mamiki mairin Audio Official 2025 Duration: 4:44 46.1K views | Jan 24, 2025 Miskito Lawana Duration: 2:44 54.9K views | Aug 14, 2020 Miskito Lawana Duration: 3:18 FE 4237 Music of the Miskito Indians of Honduras and Nicaragua, recorded by David Blair Stiffler",Mískito,Misumalpan
