6,"Rare - Understanding the Differences Between Modern Languages Descendant of Mayan, Aztec, Incan, and Misumalpan Civilizations",https://www.rarelanguage.com/post/understanding-the-differences-between-modern-languages-descendant-of-mayan-aztec-incan-and-misuma,"August 8, 2024 - Quechua-speaking communities maintain traditional weaving, music, and agricultural practices that reflect the enduring legacy of the Incan civilization. Misumalpan Languages: Misumalpan languages are central to the cultural identity of indigenous communities in Nicaragua and Honduras. Miskito, in particular, is vital for maintaining traditions, oral histories, and social practices.",Mískito,Misumalpan
